    "body": "Points 3 and 4 checked on upstream/main (after PR #1127 merged). Both are fully met:\n\n- **3. The named refusal wins over a sim gouge line.** `model_fidelity::program_tol` returns the gate's own refusal line whenever a program op is refused for its model's fidelity. The program sim (`stock_sim.rs`, `stock_sim_carry.rs`) and playback (`stock_play.rs`) judge at that tolerance, so they report \"not judged\" with the refusal and never add a gouge line. Pinned by `fidelity_copies::the_named_refusal_wins_over_a_gouge_line_the_sim_would_read`. The case: a fine part in a stock copied from a too-coarse model whose source was deleted, with the toolpath sunk 0.05 mm. The report holds only the refusal, the sim's not-judged line names it, and the eye's `target_note` is the refusal.\n- **4. Display tolerances.** `stock_view::field_view` takes `fv.tol` from `program_tol`. The machined-surface classes (`machined_classes::mesh_classes` -> `gate_tol(fv.tol, ..)`) and the viewport eyes (`ui` `trace/eye.rs:311` and `trace/cpu_eye.rs:169`, both `fv.tol`) all read that one tolerance, so on a reduced-fidelity model the colours are gated at the tightened verdict tolerance. Pinned by `fidelity_copies::the_eyes_colours_are_gated_at_the_tightened_verdict_tolerance` (field view and playback both read `DEV_TOL - excess`; full fidelity still reads `DEV_TOL`).\n\nPoint 2 is being worked now on `issue/1056-fidelity-unknown`. Decision: a pre-v59 file loads every mesh with no recorded chord as \"fidelity unknown\", and those meshes are refused by name until they are re-imported. Re-measuring is not possible without the B-rep. The PR follows.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
